Upgrade `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` to **0.19.0 or later**, then set `verbose: false` in the pool config.

```ts
// vitest.config.ts
import { cloudflareTest } from "@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers";
import { defineConfig } from "vitest/config";

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [
    cloudflareTest({
      wrangler: { configPath: "./wrangler.jsonc" },
      verbose: false, // hide verbose workerd runtime logs
    }),
  ],
});
```

If you use `cloudflarePool()` instead of `cloudflareTest()`, put `verbose: false` in that call. The 0.19.0 changelog says the option goes in either one. I'm less sure the rest of the config above exactly matches your version, so keep your existing options and just add `verbose: false`.

What this does:
- **`verbose` defaults to `true`.** Setting it to `false` hides the verbose workerd runtime output, such as caught Durable Object RPC errors.
- **TLS "peer disconnected" messages are hidden automatically in 0.19.0.** These are the `disconnected: peer disconnected without gracefully ending TLS session` stack traces that appear when tests make real `fetch()` calls. You don't need to change anything for them.
- **The pool's own debug logging is already off by default.** Since 0.14.8 it logs at INFO level. If you want those messages back while debugging, set `NODE_DEBUG=vitest-pool-workers`.

If you're on Miniflare v5 (pool 0.20.0+), the old Miniflare options `handleRuntimeStdio` and `structuredWorkerdLogs` were removed. Use `verbose` instead of trying to filter stdio yourself.

The Ludion knowledge base had no lesson on this, so the answer comes from the release notes below.

Sources:
- [vitest-pool-workers 0.19.0 release notes](https://newreleases.io/project/github/cloudflare/workers-sdk/release/@cloudflare%2Fvitest-pool-workers@0.19.0)
- [Worker disposal errors no longer fail test runs](https://releases.sh/release/rel_Y9zRdp9--a5wQBMG0Ydpq)
- [Vitest pool moves to Miniflare config shape](https://releases.sh/release/rel_82trRMVVezzHqzpOKzt2j-vitest-pool-moves-to-miniflare-config-shape)
- [Miniflare override options pruned (0.20.0)](https://releases.sh/release/rel_a7C6TTOpRodtIVBmBlw9o-workers-vitest-pool-workers-v0-20-0-removes-several-miniflare-override-options)

